1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:03,705
This is Frigi, your AI kitchen companion.

2
00:00:03,835 --> 00:00:07,667
Snap a photo of your fridge,
and Frigi finds your ingredients,

3
00:00:07,717 --> 00:00:12,230
asks what you're craving, and suggests
recipes you can cook right now.

4
00:00:12,359 --> 00:00:15,241
Creating a free account
takes about a minute.

5
00:00:15,371 --> 00:00:19,374
Frigi asks for your allergies,
diet and household size,

6
00:00:19,424 --> 00:00:23,608
so every recipe is safe for
you and makes the right amount.

7
00:00:23,738 --> 00:00:26,975
I already have an account,
so let's log in.

8
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:31,163
The home screen shows what's
in my fridge, my saved recipes,

9
00:00:31,213 --> 00:00:33,055
and what I can cook now.

10
00:00:33,185 --> 00:00:38,580
From here I can chat with Chef Frigi,
or scan my fridge and add food by hand.

11
00:00:38,709 --> 00:00:43,725
My profile keeps my preferences:
a household of two, vegetarian,

12
00:00:43,775 --> 00:00:45,498
with a peanut allergy.

13
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:49,274
Notes I leave after cooking
are used for future recipes.

14
00:00:49,403 --> 00:00:51,521
Now let's scan the fridge.

15
00:00:51,652 --> 00:00:54,707
I can add up to five
photos: the whole fridge,

16
00:00:54,757 --> 00:00:57,665
plus close-ups of the
drawers and the door.

17
00:01:00,828 --> 00:01:06,933
Our fine-tuned RF-DETR model looks for
42 kinds of ingredients in every photo.

18
00:01:07,064 --> 00:01:10,774
The photos are processed
in memory and never stored.

19
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:12,986
Here's what it found in each photo,

20
00:01:13,036 --> 00:01:16,851
with a box and a confidence
score for every item.

21
00:01:18,859 --> 00:01:23,727
Frigi merges all five photos into
one list, without duplicates.

22
00:01:23,857 --> 00:01:29,265
Items it isn't sure about, like the
water bottle and chicken, start unticked.

23
00:01:29,395 --> 00:01:32,711
I can search for anything
it missed, like rice.

24
00:01:34,562 --> 00:01:38,101
And I can tap common staples,
such as cooking oil.

25
00:01:38,231 --> 00:01:41,955
Next, Chef Frigi asks
a few quick questions.

26
00:01:42,085 --> 00:01:45,006
I'll pick Italian, and a main course.

27
00:01:46,452 --> 00:01:49,491
Then I'll type that I'm in
the mood for something spicy.

28
00:01:50,285 --> 00:01:52,956
I'll give it an hour, and cook for two.

29
00:01:54,232 --> 00:01:58,682
Recipes come from Spoonacular,
Gemini picks the best matches,

30
00:01:58,732 --> 00:02:04,087
and a rule-based safety filter checks
each one against my allergies and diet.

31
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:07,954
Each option shows the cooking
time and what I'm missing.

32
00:02:08,084 --> 00:02:10,360
Let's open the minestrone soup.

33
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:14,424
It's safety checked: no
peanuts, and vegetarian.

34
00:02:14,554 --> 00:02:18,636
Quantities scale with the servings,
I can see what's already in my fridge,

35
00:02:18,686 --> 00:02:21,804
and any missing ingredient can be swapped.

36
00:02:21,934 --> 00:02:24,710
My notes show up every time I open it.

37
00:02:25,434 --> 00:02:29,700
Start cooking opens a step-by-step
mode, showing what I need,

38
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:33,276
with built-in timers
and a note for any step.

39
00:02:35,626 --> 00:02:37,705
Let's skip ahead to the end.

40
00:02:40,576 --> 00:02:42,037
Chef's kiss!

41
00:02:42,166 --> 00:02:46,442
I can tell Frigi what to change
next time, and save the recipe.

42
00:02:46,573 --> 00:02:50,286
Back home, Chef Frigi has a
top pick from what I have,

43
00:02:50,336 --> 00:02:55,757
my fridge and stats are updated,
and my saved recipes are one tap away.

44
00:02:56,837 --> 00:03:00,366
Your fridge has ideas.
Let Frigi find them.

